                        <field name="dc_date">1080-1096 </field>
                        <field name="dc_description">This is a mostly undecorated copy of the second book of Gregory’s Homeliae in Ezechielem, written in a single-column. The manuscript is listed in the All Saints Abbey register of books from about 1100 (Min. 17, f. 306v). Onto the verso of the first leaf and the recto of the last, which perhaps were originally intended as pastedowns, there later were copied documents from the 12th century. In the 15th century this codex, like many others, received a new leather binding with metal bosses and two clasps. </field>
